.TH DICT 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Value Types"
.SH NAME
dict \- built-in dictionary value type methods
.SH DESCRIPTION
Dictionaries in y-- provide key-value mappings. Keys can be of almost any type,
including numbers, strings, and other hashable objects.
.SH METHODS
.TP
\fBget(key, [default_return])\fR -> any
Returns the value for \fBkey\fR, or \fBdefault_return\fR if the key does not exist.
.TP
\fBget_default(key, [default_value])\fR -> any
Returns the value for \fBkey\fR. If it does not exist, inserts \fBkey\fR mapped to \fBdefault_value\fR and returns it.
.TP
\fBclear()\fR -> none()
Removes all elements from the dictionary.
.TP
\fBupdate(other_dict)\fR -> none()
Updates the dictionary with key-value pairs from \fBother_dict\fR.
.TP
\fBpop([key])\fR -> any
Removes the specified \fBkey\fR and returns its value. Throws KeyError if not found.
If no key is given, removes and returns an arbitrary value.
.TP
\fBkeys()\fR -> list()
Returns a list of all keys.
.TP
\fBvalues()\fR -> list()
Returns a list of all values.
.TP
\fBitems()\fR -> list()
Returns a list of 2-element tuples, each containing a key and its value.
.TP
\fBreserve(size)\fR -> none()
Pre-allocates bucket capacity.
.SH "FUNCTIONAL METHODS"
Functional methods iterate over the dictionary's \fBkeys\fR.
.TP
\fBAll_Of / Any_Of / None_Of / One_Of (lambda)\fR -> bool()
.TP
\fBselect / reject (lambda)\fR -> dict()
Filters the keys and returns a new dictionary containing only the matching key-value pairs.
.TP
\fBmap(lambda)\fR -> list()
Maps the keys and returns a list of the mapped results.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
list(3), set(3)
